==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm}} {{term|lang=enm|crevice}} < {{etyl|fro}} {{term|lang=fro|crevace}} < {{term|lang=fro|crever||to break, burst}} < {{etyl|la}} {{term|lang=la|crepare||to break, burst, crack}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈkɹɛvɪs/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[tight]] [[hole]] or [[crease]], in a [[puss]] or [[vag]].
#: ''a tight hole or passage between a womens legs that men like to put wood into for pleasure.

